      "text": [
        ": قَرَأْتُ فِي كِتَابٍ لِأَبِي جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ إِلَى رَجُلٍ يَسْأَلُهُ أَنْ يَجْعَلَهُ فِي حِلٍّ مِنْ مَأْكَلِهِ وَ مَشْرَبِهِ مِنَ اَلْخُمُسِ فَكَتَبَ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ بِخَطِّهِ «مَنْ أَعْوَزَهُ شَيْءٌ مِنْ حَقِّي فَهُوَ فِي حِلٍّ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1660 - It is narrated from Ali ibn Mahziar, who said:\nI read in a letter from Abu Ja'far (Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Jawad (as)) to a man who asked him for permission regarding his consumption of food and drink from the Khums:\nThe Imam (as) wrote in his own handwriting:\n\"Whoever is in need of any part of my right is granted permission.\""
        ]
      }
